//! check: fail(E0804)
//! phase: resolve
//! conforms: ty.method.receiver-mode, mem.tier0.mode.mut
//!
//! wolf-lang#325 (s154): the same X1 refusal on a `mut` PARAMETER's
//! receiver. Until s154 W1002 ("`xs` is `mut`, and the body never
//! writes it") rode beside this error and offered to drop the `mut` —
//! the opposite of the fix E0804 names, and a reader who took it
//! landed on E1014. The body does write `xs`; it misspelled the
//! write, and the lint's flat scan could not see it. A mode error on
//! a use of a parameter now stands W1002 down for that parameter, so
//! this file reports exactly one diagnostic. lupin 0.1.33 says only
//! the trap here (it has no lint wave).

fn take_last[T](mut xs: List[T]) -> T ! {none} {
    xs.pop()
}

fn main() -> !int {
    var xs = List[int]()
    (mut xs).push(1)
    take_last(mut xs) else 0
}
